# Docker reads .dockerignore from the ROOT OF THE BUILD CONTEXT, not from beside the
# Dockerfile. Every image here is built with the repository root as context (the workspace
# has to be available), so this file must live here -- a copy next to a Dockerfile is
# silently ignored, and the symptom is host node_modules landing in the image and
# overwriting the symlink farm pnpm created inside it.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.githooks

# Not needed to build an image, and large.
docs
TASKS
MEMORY

# Never, under any circumstances.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
